menu "Power and wake-up"

    config APP_PIR_GPIO
        int "PIR sensor output GPIO"
        range 0 21
        default 14
        help
            Must be an RTC-capable GPIO (0-21 on the ESP32-S3) that the camera
            does not use, so that it can wake the chip from deep sleep.
            See docs/HARDWARE.md.

    config APP_PIR_WARMUP_S
        int "PIR warm-up time after power-on (seconds)"
        range 0 300
        default 45
        help
            The PIR output is unreliable right after power-up. The device
            ignores it for this long after a cold boot.

    config APP_PIR_RECHECK_S
        int "Re-check interval while the PIR output stays high (seconds)"
        range 1 60
        default 3
        help
            After an event the PIR output can stay high for several seconds.
            Instead of staying awake, the device sleeps and wakes on a timer
            to check whether the output has dropped before re-arming it.

endmenu
